plete the square on the quadratic expression ${x}^{2}+3x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last term, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1481d4a2-64b4-590a-9dbb-c39d3364bb59" :knowledge-point/title "Expressions Containing a Negative Linear Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1efce7b4-71ad-5e07-a99e-33871ea7cf78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250371} {:answer/id #uuid "c567a9d3-3724-5932-9c3c-c3e9984492be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250372} {:answer/id #uuid "f95581a1-35db-5a62-9d3b-a8e7e5d6cbbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250373} {:answer/id #uuid "e7f26459-ff44-5eb8-886b-cf8890595096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250374} {:answer/id #uuid "2ea3430a-d4de-5905-a869-f743930447fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{21}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ea3430a-d4de-5905-a869-f743930447fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{21}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250375} :a